  SIDE PREDICTION (corridor-discriminating): dressing factor S = a0_eff/a0_ref at the
  wide-binary frequency Omega_WB = 4.16e-13 s^-1 (7 kAU, 1.5 Msun; Omega_WB/H0 = 1.8e+05):
    p=0.069: S(Omega_WB) = 0.607  -> wide-binary MOND boost suppressed
    p=0.300: S(Omega_WB) = 0.114  -> wide-binary MOND boost suppressed
    p=0.500: S(Omega_WB) = 0.027  -> wide-binary MOND boost OFF (Newtonian)
    p=1.000: S(Omega_WB) = 0.001  -> wide-binary MOND boost OFF (Newtonian)
    => a detected WB anomaly at full MOND amplitude (Chae-type) would cap p <~ 0.1 and pinch the std
       corridor [0.069, ~0.1]; a WB null (Banik-type) is consistent with any corridor p. Same logic
       kills lab/atom-interferometer MOND signatures for ANY corridor p (lab Omega/H0 >~ 1e17).

===================================================================================================
VERDICT (pre-registered thresholds; both directions, full weight)
===================================================================================================
  pure freq mu_standard: SPARC +0.0263 dex (DEAD) ; solar delta_a 6.85e-22 (pass)
  pure freq mu_simple  : SPARC +0.0226 dex (DEAD) ; solar delta_a 1.49e-14 (FAIL)
  robustness of the pure-freq SPARC death (the working rule: a 'fails' needs the same rigor):
    mu_standard: vs same-shape free-a0 accel optimum 0.1976: +0.0237 ; weighted 0.1458 vs accel-best-weighted 0.1105: +0.0354 ; observed-Omega mode worse (0.2966); Ud freedom granted; Omega0 grid-interior
    mu_simple  : vs same-shape free-a0 accel optimum 0.1951: +0.0225 ; weighted 0.1343 vs accel-best-weighted 0.1105: +0.0238 ; observed-Omega mode worse (0.2806); Ud freedom granted; Omega0 grid-interior
  hybrid (dressed accel-keying): headline p=0.5 / p=1.0 penalties (std shape): +0.0020 / +0.0089 dex
  both-ways note: mild dressing IMPROVES the unweighted fit (best 0.1918 at shape=rar, p=0.30, -0.0033 vs accel best) -- at the level of known per-galaxy
  systematics (distance/inclination/M-L correlated with V_flat); NOT claimed as a detection.
  corridor std   : [0.069, 1.000] NON-EMPTY
  corridor simple: [0.593, 1.000] NON-EMPTY
  corridor rar   : [0.000, 1.000] NON-EMPTY

  BOTTOM LINE (three-way, full weight):
  (1) PURE frequency-keying is SPARC-DEAD: best variant +0.023 dex over the acceleration-keyed law
      (past the pre-registered DEAD threshold +0.020; 2.3x the ALIVE line +0.010), with the PREDICTED
      failure signature -- per-galaxy residuals
      run against V_flat (sign-flip of the control trend; a = Omega*V is the mechanism). The only
      solar-safe pure-freq shape (standard) is exactly the SPARC-dead one; the simple shape fails BOTH.
      Frequency-keying as a REPLACEMENT for acceleration-keying is excluded by the data.
  (2) The acceleration-keyed exponential-tail shape (McGaugh RAR) ALREADY passes the Door-IVb solar
      budget undressed (delta_a ~ 6e-28): the solar-reflex kill is specific to power-law-tail mu
      (F4-standard, simple) -- frequency arguments are NOT needed for solar safety in general.
  (3) For F4's OWN shape the rescue corridor is OPEN: weak frequency DRESSING of acceleration-keying,
      a0_eff = a0 [(1+Omega/H0)/(1+Omega_ref/H0)]^-p with p in [0.069, 1.0], passes the solar budget
      AND costs <0.010 dex on SPARC (p<~0.3 costs nothing at all). The Door-IVb kill of F4 is therefore
      EVADABLE by one power-law dressing factor -- at the price of a falsifiable side prediction:
      suppressed wide-binary anomaly (S_WB = 0.6 at the corridor floor, OFF for p>=0.5) and no lab-scale
      MOND signatures. A confirmed full-amplitude WB detection would pinch the corridor to ~[0.07, 0.1].

  total runtime 240.3 s
